CAT = "pllekLaw"; SEG = "LAW"
Q = [
("A 16-year-old girl needs a routine examination. Under Polish law, whose consent is required?",
 "Hers and her parent's", ["Her parent's alone", "Hers alone", "A court's in every case"],
 "Art. 32 of the Act on the Professions of Physician and Dentist and art. 17 of the Patient Rights Act require the statutory representative's consent and also the patient's own once she has turned 16."),
("A 17-year-old refuses a treatment his parents have agreed to. What does the doctor need to proceed?",
 "Guardianship court permission", ["Hospital director's approval", "Second doctor's written opinion", "Ethics committee approval"],
 "When a minor over 16 objects despite the representative's consent, the doctor needs the permission of the guardianship court, outside true emergencies."),
("Form of consent required from an adult before a planned surgical operation:",
 "Written consent", ["Oral consent", "Implied by attending", "Notarised deed"],
 "Art. 34 requires written consent for an operation or a high-risk diagnostic or treatment method, after the information set out in art. 31. Simple examinations may be agreed orally or by conduct."),
("An unconscious adult needs urgent treatment and no relative can be reached. What does Polish law allow?",
 "Treat, consulting a colleague", ["Wait for court permission", "Wait until the patient wakes", "Treat after family consent"],
 "Art. 33 allows treatment without consent when urgent help is needed and consent cannot be obtained. The doctor should consult another doctor if possible and record the circumstances."),
("When must a doctor give medical help even outside their specialty and off duty?",
 "Whenever delay risks life", ["Only while on duty", "Within their own specialty", "Only for insured patients"],
 "Art. 30 obliges a doctor to help in every case where delay could cause danger of death, serious bodily injury or serious health disorder."),
("A hospital-employed doctor refuses a procedure on grounds of conscience. What must they do?",
 "Record it and tell the superior", ["Find a substitute personally", "Tell the Patient Ombudsman", "Get the medical chamber's consent"],
 "Art. 39 lets a doctor refuse services against their conscience, except under art. 30, but they must note this in the records; an employed doctor must also notify the superior in writing beforehand. Finding a substitute is no longer required."),
("After a patient's death, who may release the doctor from medical confidentiality?",
 "Close person, unless one objects", ["Patient's insurance company", "Director of the hospital", "Nobody, under any circumstances"],
 "Art. 40 lets a close person consent to disclosure after death, unless another close person objects or the patient objected during life."),
("General period for which a Polish provider must keep medical records after the last entry:",
 "20 years", ["5 years", "10 years", "50 years"],
 "Art. 29 of the Patient Rights Act sets 20 years from the end of the year of the last entry. Exceptions include 30 years for deaths from injury or poisoning and 22 years for children under 2."),
]
